id: pm-ts-starter-75o3
title: Migrate the output_format service override from the deprecated payload-echo protocol to declineServiceOverride
description: ""
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: deprecation,sdk,services
created_at: "2026-08-04T06:34:15.053Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T06:35:09.253Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-04T06:34:45.195Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-04T06:34:45.195Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: The override declines via declineServiceOverride() rather than by returning ctx.payload by reference; the host no longer emits extension_output_format_payload_echo_deprecated in a workspace with this package installed; pm output is unchanged and is not replaced by the host envelope
resolution: Replaced the reference-identity decline with an explicit declineServiceOverride() call and removed the now-unused ServiceOverrideContext import
expected_result: "A workspace with pm-ts-starter installed emits no extension_output_format_payload_echo_deprecated warning, and pm command output is produced by the host formatter unchanged"
actual_result: Warning count for payload_echo_deprecated is 0 on stderr in a 17-package workspace; pm list --json returns items/count/filters and not the global/format/options/result envelope; all 48 unit tests pass
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T06:34:25.298Z",codex,"The old protocol inferred claim-vs-decline from reference identity: returning ctx.payload unchanged declined, returning a copy claimed it (upstream 741). That made { ...payload } a workspace-wide outage — a claimed output_format payload replaces ALL printed output, so every pm command renders as global/format/options/result with the real payload buried under .result, which is the defect this package shipped in 2026.7.28 (upstream 794). The host now offers explicit declineServiceOverride() and handleServiceOverride(result), and emits extension_output_format_payload_echo_deprecated when it falls back to inferring from reference identity. Migrated to the explicit form and dropped the now-unused ServiceOverrideContext type import. Verified functionally, not just by unit test: reinstalled into a workspace holding all 17 published packages and confirmed the deprecation warning is gone from stderr while pm list --json still returns the real payload keys (items, count, filters) and not the host envelope."
files[1]{path,scope,note}:
  index.ts,project,output_format service override migrated to declineServiceOverride
tests[1]{command,scope}:
  npm test,project
close_reason: Migrated to declineServiceOverride; deprecation warning verified gone in a 17-package workspace and pm output confirmed unchanged
body: ""
